course: dictionary
lesson: 14179
title: Who is speaking?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you who is talking and how they feel. Mommy is one of these. It is an informal word, the friendly everyday kind, that small children often use for their mother.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Lily ran into the kitchen and shouted, "Mommy, I lost my shoe!"» Lily is small, she is upset, and she wants her mother's help. The word mommy shows that clearly.
explain: A story can use mommy to make a moment feel scared or tender. «The little boy hid under the blanket and whispered, "Mommy, the thunder is so loud."» Even before the story says he is frightened, the word mommy and the thunder tell you. Ask yourself: who is speaking, and how do they feel?
fact: Mommy means mother, and it is the word a small child uses for their mom.
fact: Mommy is informal, so it is used in friendly, everyday talk rather than in formal writing.
fact: In the US and Canada, mommy is the common word; some other places say mummy for the same person.
fact: «Mommy» can also be used about mothers in general, as in «mommy bloggers» and «new mommies».
fact: A "mommy and me" class is a group where a parent and a baby go together to play and sing.
exercise: «Mommy, can you read me a story?» Who is most likely speaking? | A teacher at school | A new puppy | A shop helper | *A young child talking to their mother
exercise: «Lily ran to her mommy and gave her a hug.» Find and copy the word that means mother. | hugged | ran | her | *mommy
exercise: «The new mommies sat in a circle while their babies giggled.» Who are the mommies? | Old ladies from the village | *Mothers who have a new baby | Girls who like to giggle | Teachers at a nursery
test: «Mommy, the dog is barking!» Who is most likely speaking, and how do they feel? | A grown man at work, very calm | *A small child, worried or excited | A bird in a tree | A shopkeeper counting money
test: What is a "mommy and me" class? | *A class where a parent and their baby play together | A class where children teach their teacher | A school lesson about maths | A dance class for grown-ups only
exam: «The little girl cried, "Mommy, the lights went out!" and held her mommy's hand tightly.» What does the word mommy show about the girl? | *She is young and wants her mother because she is scared | She is a grown-up with a job | She is a teacher in a dark room | She is angry with her mother
